TEXT -928 24 Left 2 !.param CF = {IF(comp==2,1,0.001)}\n.param CF1 = {IF(comp==1,1,0)}
TEXT -1368 24 Left 2 ;comp = 0 line cappacitance is not compensated \ncomp = 1 line is compensated at end of line\ncomp = 2 line is compensated with ideal distributed elements ( no line cappacitance )
TEXT -936 64 Left 2 ;Take also a look at ilength\nIlength starts high and ends zero at uncompensated line ( because cap. current for the whole line is sourced from the slack)\nIlenght starts small and ends high at compensated line at end (because compensator is at the end (it is sourced from the line itself and not from the slack)\nIlenght is zero for ideal compensated line
TEXT -1248 256 Left 2 ;If you inspect ilength you can see that :\nIn the ideal comp. case the current is constant\nover the whole length of the line
TEXT -672 104 Left 2 ;see v(b) for the different voltages at different line positions (shape is nonlinear - sinhyperbolicus like)
TEXT -1016 264 Left 2 ;NOTE: length parameter of the line element should never be zero !!
TEXT -936 -128 Left 2 ;MAX LENGTH OF ( uncompensated and open ) line IS ABOUT 40KM\n40 * 14.829 = 593 MVAr -> 856A (at 400kV)
